course: dictionary
lesson: 15618
title: Sorting living things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Taxonomic is a long word, but the sentence around it gives clues. «The scientist used a taxonomic key to find the name of the plant.» A key helps you find a name, and the sentence is about naming a plant, so taxonomic must be about sorting and naming living things.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping in a simpler idea. «The scientist used a key for sorting living things to find the name of the plant» still makes sense, so your meaning fits. That is the check to use.
explain: The word can also be broader. «Her taxonomic system sorted the stamps by country and year.» Stamps are not living things, so here taxonomic means any careful system of naming and grouping things.
fact: Taxonomic means to do with sorting living things into named groups.
fact: The main ranks, from the largest group to the smallest, include kingdom, family, genus and species.
fact: Lions and tigers belong to the same genus, which is one reason scientists say they are closely related.
fact: A taxonomic key helps you find the name of a living thing by answering questions about its features.
fact: More broadly, taxonomic can describe any careful system of naming and grouping things, such as a stamp collection.
exercise: «The scientist used a taxonomic key to find the name of the plant.» What does taxonomic mean? | *To do with sorting living things into named groups | To do with music played in bands | To do with weather and rain | To do with cooking and baking
exercise: Which of these is a taxonomic rank? | Puddle | Colour | Garden | *Genus
exercise: «Her taxonomic system sorted the stamps by country and year.» What does taxonomic suggest here? | *A careful system of naming and grouping things | Soft and fluffy | Loud and noisy | Very hot
test: «Animals with the same shared features are placed in the same taxonomic group.» What is a taxonomic group? | *A set of living things sorted together by shared features | A tall tree | A type of weather | A party for animals
test: Why would a scientist give a new insect a taxonomic name? | To hide it from other scientists | *To give it a clear, shared name within a system | To make it sound pretty | To stop it from moving
exam: «The taxonomic key helped Mia sort the leaves into groups by shape and vein pattern.» What did the key help Mia do? | Lose the leaves | Paint the leaves | Eat the leaves | *Sort the leaves into groups by shared features
